  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "lLoIcsLjjHlkvAtdjzZ6NM81wSg=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:36:05.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "`useGetSwitchboardLink` is the hook behind the toolbar's Switchboard button, and its signature encodes a precondition:\n\n```ts\nfunction useGetSwitchboardLink(\n  document: PHDocument | undefined,\n): (() => Promise<string>) | null;\n```\n\nIt returns `null` \u2014 not a function that fails \u2014 when there is nothing to link to. Callers branch on the null and hide their button entirely.\n\n\"Remote\" is not a flag on the drive. The hook takes the selected drive, builds `DriveCollectionId.forDrive(drive.header.id)`, and looks for a matching entry in `useSyncList()`. A drive is remote precisely when a sync remote exists for its collection id. The endpoint then comes from that remote's channel config (`(remote.channel as GqlRequestChannel).config.url`), so a purely local drive with no configured remote yields `null` even though the document is perfectly real. Three things must all resolve \u2014 a remote drive, a document id, and a remote URL \u2014 or the hook returns `null`.\n\nThe token is minted at **call** time, not render time. Inside the returned async function:\n\n```ts\nconst token = user?.address\n  ? await renown?.getBearerToken({ expiresIn: 600, aud: remoteUrl })\n  : undefined;\nreturn buildDocumentSubgraphUrl(remoteUrl, document.header.id, token);\n```\n\nTwo consequences. First, the credential has a 600-second (10-minute) lifetime and is audienced to the specific remote URL, so a link generated now cannot be pasted into a chat and opened tomorrow, and cannot be replayed against a different Switchboard. Second, when no Renown user address is present the token is simply `undefined` and the URL is built anonymously rather than the call failing \u2014 so an unauthenticated user gets a link that may be rejected at the far end.\n\nBecause the function is async, wire it to a handler that awaits the URL and then opens it, rather than putting it in an `href`.\n\n_Source: packages/reactor-browser/src/hooks/use-get-switchboard-link.ts, documented at apps/academy/docs/academy/04-Reference/05-EditorsUI/01-ReactHooks.md (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:36:05.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:36:05.000Z"
    }
  },
